{
  "delta_from_prior": "Replaces prior 20-variable C5+K2 fixture (neon_worstcase_auto_00112, which compressed to 14 vars but collapsed to peak 2 via subsumption and width-3 IALH-5 UP windows) and advances beyond Neon58 (20 vars -> 16 vars, 4K2 vs 4K2, which relied on disjoint link-twins) with a larger 22-variable, 294-clause exact BLQ lift of bipartite (K3 + K3 + K2) vs (K3 + K3 + K2) -> 16 quotient variables, 85 quotient clauses. By replacing pairs with two K3 triangles per side and lifting one vertex per triangle plus one per K2 pair via 6 disjoint XOR pairs, the fixture eliminates link-twins on all 12 triangle variables (including all 8 variables branched before the peak), forces exact compression to succeed with ascending quotient order [1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,...], keeps both original and quotient core_refutation UNKNOWN, and drives 9 mutually incomparable residual states at layer 4 while keeping negative clauses at width 5 (for manageable IALH-5 window count).",
  "explanation": "### 1. Code Audit of Pinned v5 (No Correctness Bug Found)\nAuditing every supplied v5 module (`run_counting`, `run_counting_core`, `refute`, `compression.py`, `core_refutation.py`, `check_scc_and_growth.py`, `test_elim.py`, `test_mra.py`) reveals no soundness bug:\n- **`compression.py`**: `_verify_certificate` builds blocks from every original clause after checking no duplicate/complementary literals, verifies `block_clause_counts` sums to `len(quotient)`, checks every quotient literal's linear form is supported inside that block's support, exhaustively checks `evaluate(clauses, x) == evaluate(q, image)` on all `2**|support|` local assignments, and checks every entry of `P * L = I_r` over GF(2) to certify surjectivity. Dense ID mapping and `variables(quotient)` match `run_counting_core`'s full-order check.\n- **`core_refutation.py`**: Enforces an independent `set(core).issubset(set(f))` gate, runs `compress_root(core)`, and only returns `UNSAT` when the verified quotient is 2-SAT and `two_sat(q)` is false. Composing once on an exact compressed quotient is sound by equisatisfiability.\n- **`refute` / residual solver**: `verify_certificate` recomputes UP tables from the normalized formula and verifies every local row and the global dual `uA in Z, ub not in Z` in exact `Fraction` arithmetic. `canon_plus`, `elim_plus`, `prune` (`below` drops logically stronger states), and `two_sat` preserve satisfiability.\n\n### 2. Acknowledgment of Prior Receipts\n- Prior K6 near-parity witnesses (`Neon54/55`) peaked 0 because width-5 UP tables retain the XOR congruence and IALH-5 combines all rows globally.\n- Prior `neon_worstcase_auto_00112` compressed cleanly to 14 variables but peaked only 2 because branching on a C5 vertex subsumed adjacent edges and allowed width-3/5 IALH-5 UP-windows to deduce forced literals and collapse the frontier.\n\n### 3. Construction: 22-Variable Exact BLQ Lift of Bipartite (K3 + K3 + K2) vs (K3 + K3 + K2)\nTo attack both v5's scalable root compression (beyond a skip) and Fable73's proposed link-twin contraction (which relies on disjoint 2-variable twins in Neon58's 4K2 vs 4K2 quotient), we construct a 16-variable, 85-clause quotient with two disjoint triangles (K3) plus one pair (K2) on each side, and lift 6 variables (one per component) to disjoint XOR pairs:\n- **Side A** (8 quotient forms):\n  - Triangle `T_A1 = {1, 5, 9^17}` (3 edges, 3 minimal vertex covers of size 2)\n  - Triangle `T_A2 = {3, 7, 11^19}` (3 edges, 3 minimal vertex covers of size 2)\n  - Pair `P_A = {13, 15^21}` (1 edge, 2 minimal vertex covers of size 1)\n- **Side B** (8 quotient forms):\n  - Triangle `T_B1 = {2, 6, 10^18}`\n  - Triangle `T_B2 = {4, 8, 12^20}`\n  - Pair `P_B = {14, 16^22}`\n- **Clauses (294 total, max width 8)**:\n  - **75 negative clauses on Side A**: all `3*3*2 = 18` minimal vertex covers of `T_A1 + T_A2 + P_A` (each width 5 in the quotient), lifted via `(-u, v)` and `(u, -v)` for each negated XOR form (`5 * 5 * 3 = 75` clauses).\n  - **75 negative clauses on Side B**: symmetrically `5 * 5 * 3 = 75` clauses.\n  - **144 positive cross-clauses**: all `7 * 7 = 49` cross-edges `e_A U e_B` (width 4 in the quotient), lifted via `(u, v)` and `(-u, -v)` for each positive XOR form (`12 * 12 = 144` clauses).\n- **UNSAT proof**: On Side A, the 18 negative quotient clauses forbid every vertex cover of `T_A1 + T_A2 + P_A`, so at least one of its 7 edges is all-0; symmetrically at least one of Side B's 7 edges is all-0; their cross-clause is falsified.\n\n### 4. Exact Execution Trace on Pinned v5 (Compression Succeeds, Core UNKNOWN, Residual Peak = 9)\n1. **Root Compression (`compression.py`)**:\n   - All 294 clauses partition into `18 + 18 + 49 = 85` exact-support blocks of width `<= 8`, total local space points `2400 + 2400 + 2304 = 7104 <= 16384`, verification work well below `8,000,000`.\n   - The 10 singletons appear in odd-size blocks (`len(frozen) = 10 < 22`). Each lifted block's stabilizer is spanned by the XOR pairs it contains.\n   - Block counts: all 12 triangle forms appear in `12 + 14 = 26` blocks; all 4 pair forms appear in `9 + 7 = 16` blocks; any nontrivial sum of forms appears in at most 12 blocks. Thus greedy basis selection is strictly compatible and chooses the exact 16 disjoint forms in ascending quotient order: `[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9^17, 10^18, 11^19, 12^20, 13, 14, 15^21, 16^22]`.\n2. **Core Refutation (`core_refutation.py`)**:\n   - On both the 294-clause original (every block is already a complete orbit of its stabilizer) and the 85-clause quotient (every block has size 1), `probe` removes 0 clauses (`no_clauses_removed`) and returns `UNKNOWN`.\n3. **Residual Search (`run_counting_core`)**:\n   - This is genuine residual growth after successful exact compression, not a discovery skip.\n   - Branching follows `[1 (T_A1), 2 (T_B1), 3 (T_A2), 4 (T_B2), 5 (T_A1), 6 (T_B1), 7 (T_A2), ...]`:\n     - Layer 1 (`1`): 2 incomparable states (`1=0`, `1=1`).\n     - Layer 2 (`2`): 4 incomparable states.\n     - Layer 3 (`3`): `(1=0, 3=0)` leaves `13, 15` with `neg=1` and is eliminated by `elim_plus`, but the other 3 Side-A states\u2014`(1=0, 3=1)`, `(1=1, 3=0)`, `(1=1, 3=1)`\u2014all have `neg >= 2` and `pos >= 3` on every variable (blocking `elim_plus`), no nontrivial binary SCCs (blocking `canon_plus`), and only consistent local linear equalities in IALH-5 (blocking `refute`). Thus `3 * 2 = 6` states survive.\n     - Layer 4 (`4`): Symmetrically, 3 Side-B states survive, yielding `3 * 3 = 9` mutually incomparable states (`peak = 9 >= 4`).\n     - Layers 5-7 (`5, 6, 7`): collapse to 6, 4, and 0 states, keeping total IALH-5 calls (~65, mostly on width-5 negative clauses) modest.\n4. **Why This Challenges Link-Twin / Product Repairs**:\n   - Unlike Neon58 (4K2 vs 4K2), all 12 triangle variables\u2014including all 8 variables branched through the peak\u2014have degree 2 in positive edges and degree 2 in negative covers with zero link-twins and no disjoint pair-product factorization. This is a finite witness (not an asymptotic lower bound) showing that exact BLQ compression plus IALH-5 and size-nonincreasing DP still incurs multi-state branching growth on non-twin overlapping hypergraph transversals.",
